{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1452432-finland-the-sampo-louhi-and-v\u00e4in\u00e4m\u00f6inen","id":1452432,"title":"Finland, the sampo, Louhi and V\u00e4in\u00e4m\u00f6inen","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-06-16T01:52:03-07:00","id":1452432,"title":"Finland, the sampo, Louhi and V\u00e4in\u00e4m\u00f6inen","content":"So I am running a dual vampire and changeling game over discord, where the party will visit Finland, and im gonna heavily base it around the Kalevala myths. I have most of the narrative planned out, but wanted to hear some changeling veterans what their thoughts and ideas could be.<br /> <br /> Whats happened currently, is that the vampire party has gone on an adventure to northern Finland. Game takes place in 1850, main game takes place in denmark. Its an expedition led by a gangrel elder named Thomas, who is searching for his torpid sire Ikkenai. An anonymous tip has revealed that she sleeps underneath a mining town called Rovaniemi, that has recently struck gold. The players investigate the town, and find out its being managed by the keskinin, a revenant family founded Louhi, the malkavian methuselah, and a character in the Kalevala myth.<br /> <br /> The vampires decend into the mineshafts beneath the town, oblivious yet to the revenants already there, and manage to find Ikkenai embedded in a huge chunck of gold. In her hand shes clasping the sampo <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sampo\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sampo</a>. A powerful item from finnish myth, that essentially creates gold, grain or salt out of thin air. The players put her in a body bag and snatch the sampo and return up the mine elevator, where they find the building they are in beseiged by the revenants.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Thats where the story ends so far, but the reason im even posting here is to ask some changeling veterans for advise. The basic outline is that the vampire players will hopefully defeat the revenants and return home to denmark with the sampo in their possesion. In my outline, the sampo is some form of really powerful dreaming treasure. in the kalevala myth, it was made by Ilmarinen, a smith god/demigod. Im thinking about making Ilmarinen another name for Dougal, the now dead founder of the smith house Dougal in the changeling universe.<br /> <br /> But if Ilmarinen exists, then his borther V\u00e4in\u00e4m\u00f6inen probably also exists. V\u00e4in\u00e4m\u00f6inen in the kalevala is some sort of god or demigod, although he is called the first man in the more Christianized oral traditions. This mimics the way that the Irish gods where reinterpreted as magical humans by the christian irish, which is where the Tuatha de Danaan came from.<br /> <br /> So if a V\u00e4in\u00e4m\u00f6inen exists in world of darkness, what would he be? A Tuatha de Danaan? Or just a really really ancient Sidhe? Maybe even the first Sidhe, given how he's called the first man in the Kalevala. Im leaning a bit more on the Sidhe interpretation, since V\u00e4in\u00e4m\u00f6inen leaves Finland and sails into the sunset when Christianity comes in the story. Micking how the Sidhe left for arcadia.<br /> <br /> If he is a Sdihe, what house would he be? I dont know too much about the various houses. V\u00e4in\u00e4m\u00f6inen is both a powerful warrior, magician and most important a singer.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Another important question is, how would the changelings in Denmark react, if the vampires suddenly come into possession of the sampo, a dreaming artefact of such power. Im imagining a lot of conflict or open war even, but I need some ideas.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25428-ebtard","name":"Ebtard","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}